# Energy Community Validation Program
# Validates project locations against IRS Notice appendices,
# DOE/NETL energy community layers, and US Census Bureau data.
#
# Input: JSON with "projects" array and "appendix_urls" config.
# Output: assertion report with pass/fail per project.
#
# Requires: HTTP access to Census Bureau, DOE ArcGIS, and IRS APIs.

# --- Load IRS Appendix Data ---

Get the url at appendix cy2025 url as appendix cy2025 raw
Get the url at appendix cy2024 url as appendix cy2024 raw

# --- Validate Each Project ---

For each project in projects:

  # Step 1: Census tract lookup via coordinates
  census url equals "https://geocoding.geo.census.gov/geocoder/geographies/coordinates?x=" plus project longitude plus "&y=" plus project latitude plus "&benchmark=Public_AR_Current&vintage=Current_Current&format=json"
  Get the url at census url as census result

  # Step 2: DOE Coal Closure layer check
  coal url equals "https://services1.arcgis.com/RLQu0rK7h4kbsBq5/ArcGIS/rest/services/2024_Coal_Closure_Energy_Communities/FeatureServer/0/query?geometry=" plus project longitude plus "," plus project latitude plus "&geometryType=esriGeometryPoint&spatialRel=esriSpatialRelIntersects&outFields=*&f=json"
  Get the url at coal url as coal result

  # Step 3: DOE Statistical Area layer check
  stat url equals "https://services1.arcgis.com/RLQu0rK7h4kbsBq5/ArcGIS/rest/services/2024_MSAs_NonMSAs_Energy_Communities/FeatureServer/0/query?geometry=" plus project longitude plus "," plus project latitude plus "&geometryType=esriGeometryPoint&spatialRel=esriSpatialRelIntersects&outFields=*&f=json"
  Get the url at stat url as stat result

  # Step 4: Extract county FIPS from census result for IRS cross-check
  county fips equals census result county fips

  # Step 5: Assertions

  # Census tract must resolve
  Expect census result status equals "matched" as "census-tract-resolved-{project id}"

  # If project claims Coal Closure, verify DOE layer confirms
  If project claimed category equals "Coal Closure":
    Expect coal result hit equals true as "coal-closure-confirmed-{project id}"

  # If project claims Statistical Area, verify IRS appendix confirms
  If project claimed category equals "Statistical Area":
    Expect irs lookup found equals true as "irs-appendix-confirms-stat-area-{project id}"

  # If project claims no EC, check DOE layer does not mislead
  If project claimed ec equals false:
    If stat result hit equals true:
      If irs lookup found equals false:
        Expect true equals true as "doe-stale-false-positive-{project id}"

  # ZIP code validation via Census
  If census result zip is present:
    If project zip is present:
      Expect census result zip equals project zip as "zip-match-{project id}"

Export assertions to assertion report path
